        "body": "One win does not wash away a month of damage, but it does at least quiet the noise for a night. <strong>The Blue Jays' 5-2 win over the Nationals on July 29 snapped the wobble and gave them a small jolt of life.</strong> At 50-59 and fifth in the AL East, they still sit 14.5 games back, a hard reality no hot stretch can hide. The offense has leaned on George Springer's resurgence, the one bat lately that gives this lineup some edge and some lift at the deadline. But the margin remains thin, the climb steep. <strong>Tonight brings the Cardinals to town at 7:07 p.m. ET - and Toronto has to turn a single good result into something sturdier.</strong>",
