        "body": "The noise is all about the future now, and Toronto has plenty to sort out. <strong>The Kawhi Leonard trade remains on ice while the league's Clippers investigation drags on</strong> - a messy, high-wire situation that could still reshape the roster if the league finally clears the path. The Raptors are sitting in 3rd in the Atlantic Division, but the real ledger is the offseason board: who stays, who goes, and whether they keep adding swing pieces around Scottie Barnes and Immanuel Quickley. Christian Koloko's one-year move to New Orleans trims another old branch from the tree, while the announced training camp and preseason schedule gives this group a clock and a deadline. <strong>For Toronto, the next tell is simple: does the Leonard saga break one way before camp opens, or does this front office pivot to Plan B?</strong>",
